0109-venus-surface-life-trace: diagnostic only. Boot-arg surftrace=1 (read once) prints "SURFTRACE:" lines for the life of screen-sized
surfaces (width >= 1000 and height >= 2000): each user taken and given back (SweetSurface.cpp get, put), each client release (trapDetach,
trapRelease, clientClose), each free, every 2 seconds how many are alive and how much is wired, and the GPU's import, close and reap of
them (RedwoodGPU.cpp). For the 1440x3200 IOSurface that backboardd makes every frame and never frees (SWEET_SURFACE_WIRED_MAX reached,
creates fail with 0xe00002bd). One static counter caps the output at 4000 lines. Nothing changes without the boot-arg.
Base: 0108 (SweetSurface.cpp, with 0107) and the 0106 state of RedwoodGPU.cpp.

